#ASSERT `Under section 391(5), is the information a trade secret` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- SEAT13c s391(5) no economic value from secrecy: Guide "means"
#ASSERT `Under section 385(2), does the section bar the proceedings for want of the consent of the Attorney General` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT13d s385(2) no consent of the Attorney General: barred
#ASSERT `Under section 380.2(3), may the court vary the conditions prescribed in the order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT13e s380.2(3) court that made the order, application, heard, changed circumstances
#ASSERT `Under section 383(2), does the burden of proof of a bona fide intention lie on the accused` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT13f s383(2) the burden of proof of a bona fide intention lies on the accused
#ASSERT `Under section 382.1(3), is the act saved from being an offence under section 382.1` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT13g s382.1(3) the act is authorized by a federal Act
#ASSERT `t whether13` (`Under section 381, is what I did the offence of using the mails to defraud, and what are its class and punishments` TRUE TRUE FALSE 5000 6 FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT13h s381 I used the mails for a scheme to deceive the public: the offence
#ASSERT `Under section 462.47, am I justified in telling the police or the Attorney General what I suspect` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- SEAT14a s462.47 I told the police facts I reasonably suspect, despite section 241 of the Income Tax Act  -- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was EQUALS JUST TRUE; SCENARIO: | I misread "but subject to section 241 of the Income Tax Act" as "despite" and set "the Income Tax Act prevents it" to TRUE. The text makes the justification subject to s241, so with s241 preventing disclosure the answer is not JUST TRUE. The corrected case (s241 does not prevent it) is SEAT14a2 and passes. SEAT14a is left fail; Guide section 5, 'Rulings on negatives and legal effects', 'In short': NOTHING where the text 'is silent' (a bar or an 'only if' makes a case JUST FALSE when unmet; it does not by itself grant when met)
#ASSERT `Under section 462.47, am I justified in telling the police or the Attorney General what I suspect` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT14a2 s462.47 same facts but section 241 of the Income Tax Act does not prevent my disclosure (added after SEAT14a was found to misread "subject to section 241")
