#ASSERT `Under section 487.2, is it an offence to publish the location of the place searched or the identity of a person without consent before a charge is laid` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT17a s487.2 published the location of a place searched, no consent, no charge laid
#ASSERT `Under section 487.093(1), must the person executing a search warrant give me a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1, or affix them` 487 "(1)" TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT17b s487.093(1) a person present in control: copy and Form 5.1
#ASSERT `Under section 487.09(1)(c), on what day does the one year end after which my bodily substances must be destroyed` (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS (Date 1 3 2026)   -- SEAT17c s487.09(1)(c) one year after the discharge
#ASSERT `Under section 488.02(3), what is the last day on which I may apply for an order that the document not be disclosed` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS (Date 11 1 2025)   -- SEAT17d s488.02(3) 10 days after receiving the notice
#ASSERT `Under section 490(2), what is the last day on which the thing seized may be detained without a further order` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS (Date 30 6 2025)   -- SEAT17e s490(2) 180 days after the seizure
#ASSERT `Under section 490.019, must I comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act because I was served with a notice in Form 53` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT17f s490.019 served with Form 53, in the period, no exemption order
#ASSERT `Under section 487.0552(1), am I guilty of an offence for failing to comply with an order or summons to report and give DNA samples` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT17g s487.0552(1) failed to comply with a DNA reporting order, no reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `Under section 490(2), is the detention of the thing seized barred because more than 180 days have passed since the seizure` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 1 7 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT17h s490(2) day 181, no application, no order, no proceedings: barred
#ASSERT `Under section 490.0312, am I guilty of an offence for failing to advise a police service` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT18a s490.0312 failed to advise a police service, no reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `Under section 490.02911(2), must I advise a police service of a change in address` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT18b s490.02911(2) I am in Canada: change of address must be advised
#ASSERT `Under section 490.02911(2), did I advise a police service of the change in address within seven days after the change` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 8 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT18c s490.02911(2) advised on day 7: within seven days
#ASSERT `Under section 490.7, is the property barred from being disposed of until thirty days have expired` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 30 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT18d s490.7 disposed of 29 days after the order: barred
#ASSERT `Under section 490.41(3), may the court decide not to order the forfeiture because it would be disproportionate` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT18e s490.41(3) forfeiture would be disproportionate
#ASSERT `Under section 490.2(2), must a judge order the property forfeited because the accused has died or absconded, subject to sections 490.3 to 490.41` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- SEAT18f s490.2(2) the accused has not died or absconded: Guide "if the judge is satisfied"
#ASSERT `Under section 491.2(5), is the photograph, certificate, affidavit or solemn declaration barred from being received in evidence against me` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT18g s491.2(5) no copy and no notice given to me: barred
#ASSERT `Under section 490.022(1), on what day does my obligation to comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act begin` (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS (Date 1 1 2026)   -- SEAT18h s490.022(1) one year after service
#ASSERT `Under section 492.1(6), is a tracking device warrant valid for up to one year for an organized crime or terrorism offence` (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 1 1 2026) 467.12 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- SEAT18i s492.1(6) criminal organization offence: 365 days
#ASSERT `Under section 487.0552(1), what is the longest term of imprisonment in years if I am prosecuted by indictment for failing to comply` TRUE EQUALS JUST 2   -- #370c s487.0552(1) L9633-9635 (answers scenario 370's punishment half, asked in the seat) failing to comply with a DNA reporting order, prosecuted by indictment: two years
